# Application Standards

## Candidate criteria

If workspace-root `.career-pipeline.yml` is missing, stop and point the user at `.career-pipeline.yml.example` / `career-pipeline-init`.

Read workspace-root `.career-pipeline.yml` before assessing any role:

- `compensation.salary_floor` (respect `equity_counts_toward_floor`)
- `preferences.work_mode` and `preferences.location_notes`
- `search.target_roles` / `also_consider` / `flag`

Flag violations; the user may still choose to proceed. Do not unilaterally skip roles.

## Resume contact and links

When building or updating resume / cover letter HTML from `.career-pipeline.yml`:

- Use `contact.email` (required). Include `contact.phone` only when present; never invent a number.
- If `links` is present and non-empty, render each `{ label, url }` as a header **icon chip** on the right of the contact row (`contact-icons` / `icon-chip`), matching the design samples. Set `title` from `label`. Choose a simple SVG from label or URL host (LinkedIn, GitHub, globe for site/portfolio). Use the design accent fill color.
- Omit the icon group entirely when `links` is missing or empty.

## Folder layout (submissions)

Under `submissions/<Company>/<Role>/`:

- `email/` — user-exported mail only (no in-plugin mailbox sync)
- `application/` — analysis, cover letter, resume, full package, job post exports
- `interview - 1st`, `interview - 2nd`, … — created on demand by `career-pipeline-create-interview-prep`
- `offer/` — created on demand by `career-pipeline-analyze-offer` (user packet + offer analysis)

After `career-pipeline-accept-job`, that tree lives under `career/<Company>/<Role>/` with `onboarding/`, `relocation/`, `reviews/`, `issues/`, and `leaving/` added. Do not keep a duplicate under `submissions/`.

## Resume versioning

- Copy the latest export from `design/exports/`
- Resolve the resume filename from `naming.application.resume` (`pattern` + `extension`); preserve that filename exactly when copying into `application/`
- Never rename the resume when copying into application folders

## Artifact naming

Resolve each artifact from `.career-pipeline.yml` `naming.*.pattern` and `naming.*.extension` (tokens and filename-safe cleanup: plugin `docs/config.md`). Filename = `{resolved-pattern}.{extension}`. Cover letter editable HTML is always `{basename}.html`; configured `extension` is the print/export sibling.

## Commits

- All application files belong in the repo; no gitignore exclusions for application artifacts
- Commit message format: `Add <Company> application — <Job Title>`
- Only commit when the user explicitly requests it

## Equity

When equity/RSU appears in a posting or offer, quote it verbatim and apply `compensation.equity_counts_toward_floor` plus optional `compensation.notes`. Do not invent a separate equity essay path.
